                                    // copy: the disk's keeping
                                    // stands untouched, and the
                                    // stick gains the thing
                                    // under the name it stands
                                    // under here. Where the
                                    // stick already holds a
                                    // thing of that name — or a
                                    // picture already stands in
                                    // its one picture place —
                                    // the press is refused in
                                    // plain words in the window
                                    // and nothing is
                                    // overwritten, Stone 40's
                                    // discipline for a name that
                                    // already stands; where no
                                    // stick stands, or the stick
                                    // is itself this computer's
                                    // keeping, the press is
                                    // answered plainly the same
                                    // way. The outcome stands
                                    // as the exchange's word
                                    // (the desk's 492) on the
